    advDockModeHint: "Panel: fused to the screen edge. Pill: floating capsule with a gap from the edge.",
    advDockOpacity: "Opacity",
    advDockBlur: "Blur",
    advDockLookNote: "Blur is done by the compositor behind the Dock (it also blurs windows underneath); its strength is set in the compositor. Off in Performance mode. Requires the Dock to be enabled.",
    barGlass: "Glass mode",
    barGlassHint: "Makes every OozeShell window (bar, islands, popups, tooltips, notifications) translucent, with optional blur behind. Independent from Pill mode; the Dock keeps its own opacity and blur.",
    barGlassOpacity: "Opacity",
    barGlassBlur: "Blur behind",
    barGlassBlurHint: "The blur is done by the compositor (ext-background-effect, Quickshell 0.3+), so it blurs the windows underneath, not just the wallpaper. Its strength is set in the compositor. On niri add a layer-rule with background-effect { xray false } — see docs/GLASS.md. Off in Performance mode.",
    barGlassSeam: "Join gap (no blur)",
    barGlassSeamHint: "Pixels (px) without blur where a panel meets the bar. The compositor's blur also samples the dark bar next to it and leaves a shadow line at the join; this strip hides it. Raise it if you still see the line, 0 turns it off.",
    barGlassFloatHint: "With the regular bar, Glass makes the bar float and detaches popups and tooltips from it (no joining curves). With Islands they still grow out of their island.",
    barFloatWin: "Floating windows",
    barFloatWinHint: "Detaches popups, panels and tooltips from the bar so they float with a small gap, without joining curves. Works with or without Glass mode.",
    barFloatWinPerfHint: "Performance mode is on: windows float meanwhile, with no fused panels. Turning it off restores your preference.",
    barFloatWinPerfIslandsHint: "Performance mode does not detach windows in Islands or Pill without Glass: they still emerge from their island.",
    barFloatWinIslandsHint: "With Islands or Pill mode, windows keep growing out of their island or pill.",
